#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e16935-1003-52ed-a03b-f4c61dd870d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281751} {:answer/id #uuid "264a88bc-6062-5e3b-9a17-7a92ed55ba6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282024} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf06f2c-9f8f-538b-8f01-0758002d1584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10+10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282087} {:answer/id #uuid "5f45f379-dd47-579f-966c-3906aef12d7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282491} {:answer/id #uuid "719a6e30-a3a3-51da-9f47-cbd0d927b100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f45f379-dd47-579f-966c-3906aef12d7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282491} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3b1957c-b96b-5d85-8ee8-bf171f645eb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ffd9d977-ab54-5f18-98fb-c284e3e5b28b" :question/math-academy-id "q-16419" :question/problem "If $z=5+5\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=5+5\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=5,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(5) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=5+5\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=5-5\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(5+5\\text{i})+(5-5\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(5+5)+\\text{i}(5-5) \\\\  & =10+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a6e2723-1d96-59f0-9ce8-1086dbae82be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "97\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282324} {:answer/id #uuid "988ae48c-0346-5d01-9514-34a4b4841eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283008} {:answer/id #uuid "a395c26d-5b19-522a-a755-4f809cfa866c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283114} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc5556d-0f68-51f8-ad0f-405b5cda6250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "97" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283476} {:answer/id #uuid "d33c6f49-90ce-5f06-aede-23fd08c90bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccc5556d-0f68-51f8-ad0f-405b5cda6250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "97" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283476} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6d807f4-cf50-5ea5-a6ac-a321fddfc003" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4891bd7-301f-542e-bf98-c65b22eb754e" :question/math-academy-id "q-16423" :question/problem "Given that $z=4+9\\text{i}$, calculate $z\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=4+9\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=4,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=9,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =16+81 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=4+9\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=4-9\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(4+9\\text{i})(4-9\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+(4)(-9)\\text{i}+(4)(9)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(9)^{2} \\\\  & =16-36\\text{i}+36\\text{i}-(-1)(81) \\\\  & =16+81 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01599038-7fa1-5afe-a124-32486980db61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281699} {:answer/id #uuid "094a0436-bb98-5af8-8458-8b8973d56489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281771} {:answer/id #uuid "1edfa3f9-dec2-598c-8e3c-7d00d0bf3742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{36}{41}+\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281965} {:answer/id #uuid "323d7b35-d6d0-5feb-94bc-bfcb12c5c230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{36}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282141} {:answer/id #uuid "60789803-7419-5718-9d75-986c99c7bf03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{41}+\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "094a0436-bb98-5af8-8458-8b8973d56489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281771} :answer-field/id #uuid "4808f53c-9dff-528d-a08d-990f1659c668" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e45dca1-bb14-5a43-81c1-494f270d1180" :question/math-academy-id "q-16433" :question/problem "$\\frac{9\\text{i}}{-5+4\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-5+4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-5-4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-5-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9\\text{i}}{-5+4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{9\\text{i}}{-5+4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-5-4\\text{i}}{-5-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-45\\text{i}-36{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{5}^{2}-{4}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-45\\text{i}-36(-1)}{{5}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36-45\\text{i}}{25+16} \\\\  & =\\frac{36-45\\text{i}}{41}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{36-45\\text{i}}{41}=\\frac{36}{41}-\\frac{45}{41}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8434a84-5ef1-505b-a2c7-d42809c26959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401560} {:answer/id #uuid "386a0708-44f8-5648-9834-907d2d7fef7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401561} {:answer/id #uuid "f019f459-9c8d-5bca-ac2e-8bf08a5f03f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401562} {:answer/id #uuid "1362416b-6b2e-5b41-8cce-b430bb96c908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401563} {:answer/id #uuid "c489543f-9ba5-563a-8700-e139b5d4d02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1362416b-6b2e-5b41-8cce-b430bb96c908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401563} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9fd9c31-b922-5bc4-b3d4-983574117b6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8cb21ae0-f2f0-5250-97c3-5094275c61e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-16465" :question/problem "For the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{20}=1$, find the lengths of its major and minor axes." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-1$ and $k=-3,$ so the center is located at $(-1,-3).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=5$ and ${b}^{2}=20.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=5,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=20,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=2\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096708 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Y-Intercepts of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c70e801-fd99-586e-ad50-fca199a9d991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281802} {:answer/id #uuid "99578261-0e54-5ddf-9cbe-2131732d1331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283022} {:answer/id #uuid "b33f1a06-1ff7-5054-9b68-11c4a5d9ab9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283244} {:answer/id #uuid "cacc8365-ba97-5758-a9a1-2e6465cbb4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283463} {:answer/id #uuid "fca7c681-e646-5b9c-9404-16ca07e77a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b33f1a06-1ff7-5054-9b68-11c4a5d9ab9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283244} :answer-field/id #uuid "e67bd542-ad74-5a89-8312-e4d33f763205" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a86ebeb5-18d1-5f84-a46f-2e3c446ad259" :question/math-academy-id "q-165433" :question/problem "![](images/61/616116b9e5cf137c526b11dc5ce1647cd8f9cbd3a652be6dade9a8769467c27c.png)\n\nWhat is the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(5,15)$ and passes through the point $(2,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(5,15)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x-5)^{2}=4p(y-15).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(2,6),$ we substitute $x=2$ and $y=6$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2-5)^{2} & =4p(6-15) \\\\ 9 & =4p(-9) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5)^{2} & =-(y-15).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-5)^{2} & =-(y-15) \\\\ 25 & =-y+15 \\\\ y & =15-25 \\\\ y & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7df2ec3-6138-5b84-864b-a856c28b9747" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Y-Intercept of a Transformed Exponential Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2432ea9b-d21e-5a51-8b4f-b55efb6bd9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282007} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cbd424-f3a1-5a84-9361-9c96b4e6b238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283363} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a95d55-7f7d-5b96-9047-fa934daf6737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283384} {:answer/id #uuid "d086b4fb-f27d-5ee6-8b86-c8312d6c931f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283508} {:answer/id #uuid "e1eef64f-270a-5804-b5e7-c47f798b2c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2432ea9b-d21e-5a51-8b4f-b55efb6bd9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282007} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2a3e1d9-5970-53e9-bf11-467d12c1c3c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7bdbdc9-a156-56fb-bd3a-e5d66cea5150" :question/math-academy-id "q-165971" :question/problem "Determine the $y$-intercept of $y={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5x-2}+1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5(0)-2}+1 \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-2}+1 \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+1 \\\\  & =4+1 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a508c1-2379-590f-85f5-386a1990f137" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the x-Intercepts of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4f3d642-de3f-54d5-aede-eba21e11be92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no $x$-intercept" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401567} {:answer/id #uuid "e9df0568-122c-5b6d-9b84-d5caa3cabe43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401568} {:answer/id #uuid "dc20f4f3-9c00-5d0b-920a-7a632bc6b622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401569} {:answer/id #uuid "20209ee4-eb61-55e6-aa7a-3caa61c198e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401570} {:answer/id #uuid "73f81d60-d0cf-5e03-8299-56a8163c5850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc20f4f3-9c00-5d0b-920a-7a632bc6b622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401569} :answer-field/id #uuid "160e9ede-f9e3-593e-8295-6afb981450c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fca3c3f7-188d-5506-9818-be66c0607803" :question/math-academy-id "q-16642" :question/problem "Calculate the points where the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4}{9} & =1 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}+16 & =36 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2} & =20 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =\\frac{20}{9} \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{20}{9}} \\\\ x & =3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(3-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)$ and $(3+\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a508c1-2379-590f-85f5-386a1990f137" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the x-Intercepts of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68d1becd-834d-5b48-8a24-ab24c44b2a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm 3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282587} {:answer/id #uuid "afa421db-4a22-51a3-be0c-e9fc90b73e74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\pm 3\\sqrt{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283208} {:answer/id #uuid "c457d605-1675-5574-80ea-b02b08321902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm \\sqrt{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283402} {:answer/id #uuid "dd86044f-0ff0-52c7-a162-ab49488967da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no $x$-intercept" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283623} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f0a86d-eee6-5481-8c8b-c4472e4f786e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\pm \\sqrt{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afa421db-4a22-51a3-be0c-e9fc90b73e74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\pm 3\\sqrt{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283208} :answer-field/id #uuid "037f6be5-b84d-5111-bcea-8a60d5bd8ffd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad41fa9c-427e-53d4-84ac-70d9cefddf98" :question/math-academy-id "q-16647" :question/problem "Calculate the points where the ellipse $4(x-3)^{2}+9{y}^{2}=72$ intercepts the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-3)^{2}+9{y}^{2} & =72 \\\\ 4(x-3)^{2}+9\\cdot {0}^{2} & =72 \\\\ 4(x-3)^{2} & =72 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =18 \\\\ (x-3) & =\\pm \\sqrt{18} \\\\ (x-3) & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at $(3-3\\sqrt{2},0)$ and $(3+3\\sqrt{2},0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c21c1eca-cf80-56bd-9f44-aab7989cb210" :knowledge-point/title "The Root of a Transformed Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e3c4350-ac40-5ff9-8a09-56250f13df9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282483} {:answer/id #uuid "70df90bc-b41f-53c9-ace7-14daa143036c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282655} {:answer/id #uuid "7268a672-d5da-52a3-9409-8ef22f8f8007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282668} {:answer/id #uuid "aca0a2ac-645b-50e7-b37a-d45fee6649df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283184} {:answer/id #uuid "da63b78c-2331-50f1-a0b0-42446f4d812e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aca0a2ac-645b-50e7-b37a-d45fee6649df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283184} :answer-field/id #uuid "85e23c55-3564-5b82-9ccb-0a33e23e13b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b15a7e63-b8ab-5083-9941-85a35f55da3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-166549" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)={log}_{2}⁡(4-2x)+1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x)$, we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n{log}_{2}⁡(4-2x)+1=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}⁡(4-2x)+1 & =0 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(4-2x) & =-1 \\\\ {2}^{{log}_{2}⁡(4-2x)} & ={2}^{-1} \\\\ 4-2x & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -2x & =-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{7}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=\\frac{7}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217152 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fa86dd3-3bb3-54d5-8940-5dc07ae4c99f" :knowledge-point/title "Exponential Growth Functions With Horizontal and Vertical Shifts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99ad0535-275d-5569-9ac3-9c14fa99a5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/11/11ec7fbc5908465c69f2bea959f6164ab115b30f767260652658649bc7e9cf65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389576} {:answer/id #uuid "c97a6005-11ae-5bc5-9656-338b6e77d9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/83ee71cbcf2456ce581e91624155d9528903c56c491debdbc3de392e7799720a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389577} {:answer/id #uuid "5731da45-7ae4-5755-be3e-c71696c160cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/1065343505af421e2a1fc06c9733dfc3a2354842daec12ac4bcc2d7935c8b1ab.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389578} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb0e59b-b1ef-56d1-b881-1e0d2f7f1ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c2d437d87e38ef73849987c358bc00fd589535c5045b193cdfa54ecc9601f37e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389579} {:answer/id #uuid "18a565a2-df94-546c-9080-271b1c1bf113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8ccfcbd3042f4504a2df8f51c82df1238fdc6c479fa99f6b4691543f8685ffba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6eb0e59b-b1ef-56d1-b881-